notes.body:
For the preferences and profiles side of this, what if we leveraged the fact that we ship with a JSON parser and dumper? We could store something like the following instead of gui.layout_type and gui.layout_content_[1-3].

    { "version": 2, "hsplit": { "PLIST": null, "vsplit": { "PDETAILS": null, "PBYTES": null } } }

or 

    { "version": 2, "hsplit": [ "PLIST", { "vsplit": [ "PDETAILS", "PBYTES" ] } ] }

This would map roughly to the way layouts are structured with QSplitter and allow for more flexible layouts. It should also let us map between this and the current preference variables without too much trouble.

